# The ETag compared by value: the row's incarnation is ignored, so after a purge
# an epoch value that recurs matches an old activation's write. Clean against
# OnlySupersededRefused, ReadPositionHonest and StaleEpochNeverAppends in this
# instance; kept because production compares the ETag, which a recurring value
# never matches.
MODULE: OnlySupersededRefusedEtagByValue
TARGET: OnlySupersededRefused
CLASS: Invariant
EXPECT: clean (a redundancy check: the guard is implied in the model and kept for the reason in LiveAdvanceDesign.md)
SUMMARY: the row compare ignores the incarnation
PERTURBS: ClaimRow, ClaimBump, OtherPartitionBump
BOUNDS: WithRecreate = TRUE, WithBatch = FALSE, MaxWindows = 1

--- FIND
RowUnmoved(a) == seen[a] = rowEpoch /\ seenInc[a] = rowInc
RowHolds(a) == rowEpoch = epoch[a] /\ seenInc[a] = rowInc
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: compared by value.
RowUnmoved(a) == seen[a] = rowEpoch
RowHolds(a) == rowEpoch = epoch[a]
--- END